⁡({y}^{2})\\,j,\\,∇\\cdot G=3y\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505751 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2c768058-b351-51d4-a894-a96f2a63f5a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505751 #edb/ref 1074 "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following  linearity properties for divergence:\n\n- $∇\\cdot (kF)=k∇\\cdot F$\n\n- $∇\\cdot (F+G)=∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (3F+2G) & =∇\\cdot (3F)+∇\\cdot (2G) \\\\  & =3∇\\cdot F+2∇\\cdot G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\cdot F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}-2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (3F+2G) & =3∇\\cdot F+2∇\\cdot G \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}-2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}))+2\\cdot (3y\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}-6y\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2})+6y\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505757 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186505670 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505757 #edb/ref 1069 "q-131291" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505757 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505757 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $F(x,y,z)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,x{z}^{3},{z}^{2}⟩$ and $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}z,$ calculate $∇\\cdot (f\\,F).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505757 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "37458a2a-1dd8-5f4b-97d7-084609fd0a20" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505757 #edb/ref 1074 "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot (f\\,F)=f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇\\cdot F$ and $∇f.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =⟨2xz,0,{x}^{2}⟩, \\\\ ∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{z}^{3})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({z}^{2})=\\frac{1}{x}+2z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (f\\,F) & =f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f \\\\  & ={x}^{2}z(\\frac{1}{x}+2z)+⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,x{z}^{3},{z}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨2xz,0,{x}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =xz+2{x}^{2}{z}^{2}+2xz\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+{x}^{2}{z}^{2} \\\\  & =xz+3{x}^{2}{z}^{2}+2xz\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\  & =xz(1+3xz+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505762 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186505715 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505762 #edb/ref 1069 "q-131243" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505762 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505762 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $∇\\cdot (-4F)$ for the vector field $F$ where\n\n$$\nF={x}^{2}yz\\,i+({y}^{3}-y)\\,j-xy{z}^{2}\\,k.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505762 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4c942870-19a7-5088-91ca-fc84364e3087" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505762 #edb/ref 1074 "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following  linearity properties for divergence:\n\n- $∇\\cdot (kF)=k∇\\cdot F$\n\n- $∇\\cdot (F+G)=∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (-4F)=-4∇\\cdot F.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\cdot F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}yz)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{3}-y)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(-xy{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =2xyz+3{y}^{2}-1-2xyz \\\\  & =3{y}^{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (-4F) & =-4∇\\cdot F \\\\  & =-4\\cdot (3{y}^{2}-1) \\\\  & =4-12{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505846 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186505890 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505846 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0017b014-af13-5dd7-825c-45a467efd98c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505846 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186366829 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505857 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2ef3bb86-4410-5f70-b715-2125b5cff05f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505857 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186505757 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505871 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186505884 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505871 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5eb56b94-7439-5882-b527-53d920358a26" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505871 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186179909 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505884 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186505846 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505884 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a7f009b6-e8bd-5ad5-a7ce-b0ae93ab904e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505884 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186505751 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505890 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186505857 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505890 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cff4c98e-4515-5b93-aac2-f02400e27f42" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505890 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186505762 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
